[{:db/id 17592186092186 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2997dd93-b478-5bad-935c-182c80540138"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2997dd93-b478-5bad-935c-182c80540138" :question/id #uuid "2997dd93-b478-5bad-935c-182c80540138" :question/math-academy-id "q-10091" :question/problem "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+2z=0 \\\\ x+2y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x+y+z=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-1(1-9)+2(1-6) \\\\  & =+8-10 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 & -5 \\\\ -1 & -6 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -6 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -8 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -8 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 9 \\\\ -\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=9,z=-\\frac{9}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e7180735-62b0-5917-9dd2-0f45d066402b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e7180735-62b0-5917-9dd2-0f45d066402b" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7180735-62b0-5917-9dd2-0f45d066402b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-546c8e95-b26b-5ff9-83d6-638b399b687a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2d344f8-2327-5d63-96e1-0bdf947cb05c" "answer-922397fb-a6df-5cdc-b3c4-40ed001f749e" "answer-92176233-f61a-5a1f-a96a-0e59d129daf0" "answer-546c8e95-b26b-5ff9-83d6-638b399b687a" "answer-854c87f7-583e-578a-92c5-d3db59792427"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2d344f8-2327-5d63-96e1-0bdf947cb05c" :answer/id #uuid "d2d344f8-2327-5d63-96e1-0bdf947cb05c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,y=-18,z=-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-922397fb-a6df-5cdc-b3c4-40ed001f749e" :answer/id #uuid "922397fb-a6df-5cdc-b3c4-40ed001f749e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,y=18,z=-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92176233-f61a-5a1f-a96a-0e59d129daf0" :answer/id #uuid "92176233-f61a-5a1f-a96a-0e59d129daf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=-9,z=-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-546c8e95-b26b-5ff9-83d6-638b399b687a" :answer/id #uuid "546c8e95-b26b-5ff9-83d6-638b399b687a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5}{2},y=9,z=-\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-854c87f7-583e-578a-92c5-d3db59792427" :answer/id #uuid "854c87f7-583e-578a-92c5-d3db59792427" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{5}{2},y=9,z=\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186403947 :question/problem "Consider a system of $n$ linear equations in $n$ variables, written in matrix form as $D\\,z=c.$ Here, $D$ is the non-singular coefficient matrix of the system, $z$ is the column vector containing the variables, and $c$ is the column vector containing the constants. The unique solution of the system can be found using the method shown below:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\\,z & =c \\\\ {D}^{-1}D\\,z & =c \\\\ z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c \\\\ z & ={D}^{-1}\\,c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom and right to left, what are the missing parts of the derivation?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-19f27baf-34c3-5e03-bcb6-d2509997eb57" :activity/id #uuid "19f27baf-34c3-5e03-bcb6-d2509997eb57" :activity/title "Solving Systems of Equations Using Inverse Matrices" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049392 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-100a637e-a49a-5d4a-80d2-e88a9e19ca4c" "step-42e8894e-d466-5fe7-9f98-3286e55d0c47" "step-227ec066-022a-52e9-9829-1a29de29e8db"] :activity/first-step "step-100a637e-a49a-5d4a-80d2-e88a9e19ca4c" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-100a637e-a49a-5d4a-80d2-e88a9e19ca4c" :step/id #uuid "100a637e-a49a-5d4a-80d2-e88a9e19ca4c" :step/content "question-2997dd93-b478-5bad-935c-182c80540138" :step/next "step-42e8894e-d466-5fe7-9f98-3286e55d0c47" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "st